    "body": "This was introduced in https://github.com/whatwg/html/commit/f355f4a44cb833de93a52ce37eed8cc2d5f9c8c2. The rationale seems to start at https://krijnhoetmer.nl/irc-logs/whatwg/20090113#l-261 and gives http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?%3C!DOCTYPE%20html%3E%0D%0A...%3Ciframe%20name%3Dbody%3E%3C%2Fiframe%3E%3Cscript%3Ew(document.body)%3C%2Fscript%3E as an example.\r\n\r\nIn your test `foo` is not a builtin so I'm not sure why you expect it to override that?",
